@startuml diagram
title Virtual Lab Lifecycle (L0–L4)

[*] --> dev

state "In Development" as dev <<development>>
dev : Complete tasks required at the current level

state "Evaluation Phase" as eval <<evaluation>>
eval : Coordinator checks quality and exit conditions

state "Promotion to Next Level" as prog <<transition>>
prog : Exit conditions approved; lab promoted

state "Required Modifications" as modification <<feedback>>
modification : Coordinator suggests changes

state "Operational Maintenance" as maintenance <<maintenance>>
maintenance : Maintain and monitor the lab in production

dev --> eval : request evaluation
eval --> prog : approval
eval --> modification : request changes
modification --> eval : resubmit for evaluation
prog --> dev : move to next level (L0–L3)
prog --> maintenance : lab reaches L4

note left of dev
Applies to labs in levels L0 to L3
end note

note left of maintenance
Only applies to L4 labs in operational state
end note

legend left
<<development>>  Development activities
<<evaluation>>   Quality assessment by Coordinator
<<transition>>   Advancement to next maturity level
<<feedback>>     Required revisions
<<maintenance>>  Operational upkeep for L4 labs
endlegend

@enduml
